OL,3,GNEWSA'I'm shocked doctors haven't heard
OL,4,Aof my invisible cancer'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA woman who has incurable
OL,7,Fneuroendocrine cancer is calling for
OL,8,Fgreater awareness of the rare disease,
OL,9,Fwhich she describes as an "invisible
OL,10,Fcancer".
OL,12,FRachel Wood, 55, from Shrewsbury, has
OL,13,Fcancer in her small bowel that has
OL,14,Fspread to her liver and bones. She said
OL,15,Fit took 18 months for her to be
OL,16,Fdiagnosed because healthcare
OL,17,Fprofessionals did not recognise the
OL,18,Fdisease, which can develop in the
OL,19,Fstomach, bowel, pancreas or lungs.
